      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Complete Theorem3.2 proof Sections3.3-3.5 was read, including the integer-theta support theorem3.1. The author obtains the integer case from index-argument symmetry and one-row generating functions, deforms the contour and interpolates in x. For all positive real theta he supplies absolute q-Gamma tail estimates, complex-theta holomorphy via compact-uniform domination and Morera, uniform right-half-plane boundedness for Carlson uniqueness, signature shifts and boundary dominated convergence. Theorem3.3 details are explicitly omitted by the source and are not selected. Macdonald evaluation/branching and Carlson uniqueness are established cited background."
      },
      "extra_source_paths": [
        "raw/sigma-2018-001-036/paper-001-source/sigma18-001.tex",
        "raw/sigma-2018-001-036/paper-001-source.zip"
      ],
      "statement_scope": "Exactly Theorem3.2: real q in (0,1), real theta>0, t=q^theta, positive integer N, integer nonincreasing signature lambda in GT_N and complex x nonzero with absolute value <=1. Retain the normalized ratio P_lambda(x*t^(N-1),t^(N-2),...,1)/P_lambda(t^(N-1),...,1), exact q-Gamma prefactor, and the positively oriented C-plus contour with lambda_N>M and 0<r<-pi/(2*ln(q)). Retain the logarithm convention of Remark3.4. No independent multiplicative formula, boundary classification or omitted Theorem3.3 is counted.",
      "admission_hold": false,
      "proof_complete": true,
      "contexts": [],
      "id": "1765",
