      "material_role": "selected_problem",
      "countable_problem_unit": true,
      "root_admission_required": true,
      "source_boundary_note": "The complete original Theorem 3.2 and detailed Steps 0–4 are retained for all real theta>0, integer signatures and nonzero |x|<=1. The full new integer-parameter Theorem 3.1 proof is bundled as uncounted core, including index shifts, deformation/interpolation and finite-pole control. Complete new q-Gamma tail estimates, compact-uniform holomorphy/Morera and unbounded right-half-plane Carlson bounds, boundary domination and signature shifts are supplied. Macdonald symmetry/evaluation/branching, q-binomial identities and Carlson uniqueness remain author-cited standard prerequisites. The exact C-plus contour and logarithm convention are retained. The neighboring Theorem 3.3 has explicitly omitted details and is not counted; neither multiplicative formulas nor Martin-boundary results are selected.",
